. Its platform header reported loopback MTU 65536 and socket-buffer defaults/maxima, plus a missing `/proc/sys/net/ipv4/udp_mem`; none of those diagnostics constitutes a passed probe leg.\n\n## Contract and portability disposition\n\nThere is no J7 production code to verify against §8.4 and the committed design: immediate `transport-error` plus exactly one `send-failed` on would-block/ENOBUFS, one send syscall, no `full`, no queue/retry, bounded nonblocking receive, IPv4/IPv6, source fidelity, oversize handling, or cleanup. DHT native servicing and signed-head composition are also unimplemented in this diff. Historical J0b results do not establish these production guarantees.\n\nNo new top-level conditional requires, jolt dependencies in shared cljc, or JVM behavior changes were introduced: all source and tests match the base. JVM load passed independently. Node/Dart loads, native macOS/Linux parity, and DHT/signed-head runtime acceptance remain unqualified; no pass is inferred from their absence or from the wrapper's success status.\n\nOnly this findings artifact is changed by this review. No implementation fixes were made and no supplied logs were staged. `git diff --check origin/master..HEAD` passed.\n\n## Commit status\n\nWhitespace validation with `git diff --no-index --check /dev/null collab/jolt/j7-review.findings.md` passed. The requested staging/commit command was attempted, but `git add` exited 128 before staging:\n\n```text\nfatal: Unable to create '/home/sto/ci/datomworld-j6e-linux/.git/worktrees/dw-j7/index.lock': Read-only file system\n```\n\nThe linked worktree's Git metadata is outside this session's writable roots. No commit completed; this report remains untracked at the requested path. Completing the commit requires write access to that metadata. No Git metadata or permissions were changed to bypass the restriction.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
