{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'transit|cbor|board-codec' test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc src/jolt/yin/repl/host.jolt; sed -n '600,740p' src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc; sed -n '1,200p' src/jolt/dao/host/hash.jolt\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:877:(def ^:private board-codec\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:879:  (:cbor connect/codec-profiles))\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:882:(def ^:private board-codecs\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:884:  (into [(:cbor connect/codec-profiles)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:885:        (when-let [t (:transit connect/codec-profiles)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:897:                                  :codecs board-codecs})]\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:912:  \"The board's end, printed once on its transition to stopped.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc:1054:                              :codec board-codec})]\n   replaces the refusal that caused it.\"\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n\n\n(defn open\n  \"Open a `dht:<dir>` store from its spec (`checked-spec`): the durable\n   directory store, and the `dao.space.dht` node joined over it.\n\n   Answers the two values of section 3's ownership split, and never one\n   value carrying both:\n\n   ```clojure\n   {:index-store <the generic dao.jing handle the engine is constructed\n                  with, carrying :head-fn, :recovery, :publication-policy\n                  and :retain-on-reset?>\n    :node <this composition's transport step-owner value>\n    :recovery <what the open validated, {:manifest :datoms}>\n    :publication-policy <the immutable generic policy of section 5>\n    :retain-index-on-reset? true}\n   ```\n\n   `opts`: `:key`, the publisher key `{:seed :public}`, which makes a\n   publishing node deposit its head; `:ws`, the host WebSocket seam\n   `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (yin.repl.host) the board is served and\n   dialed over; `:write-heads!`, `(fn [dir name text])`, the atomic file\n   replace `heads.edn` is written with (`dao.space.store.fs` by\n   default); `:open-store`, `(fn [dir])`, the durable directory open\n   (`dao.space.store/open` by default).\n\n   A refusal releases everything it opened, exactly once, and is\n   answered as itself whatever the release throws: before the join the\n   directory store is closed; once joined the node owns it, and closing\n   the node closes the socket and then the store.\"\n  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads! open-store]}]\n   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n                 manifest bind!]\n          :as checked} (checked-spec spec)\n         follow (checked-follow checked)\n         base ((or open-store durable/open) dir)\n         [node records]\n         (try\n           (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n                                         (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n             (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n           (let [records (heads-records dir follow)]\n             [(dht/join {:local base\n                         :peers peers\n                         :publish? publish?\n                         :bind-host bind-host\n                         :bind-port bind-port\n                         :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n                         :repair-slots default-repair-slots\n                         :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n              records])\n           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n             (quietly! #(durable/close! base))\n             (throw e)))]\n     ;; from here the node owns the store and holds a socket\n     (try\n       (let [[index-store node]\n             (compose node base checked follow records\n                      {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})]\n         {:index-store index-store\n          :node node\n          :recovery (:recovery index-store)\n          :publication-policy (:publication-policy index-store)\n          :retain-index-on-reset? true})\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (quietly! #(dht/close! node))\n         (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn follower\n  \"The head follower a composition's `node` carries, or nil when it\n   follows nothing.\"\n  [node]\n  (get node ::follower))\n\n\n(defn stop!\n  \"Initiate the head composition's exit on `session`'s node: the board's\n   server is asked to stop (`head.board/stop!`), every follow dial is\n   closed and no dial is composed again, and the node is marked\n   stopping.  Performs no other I/O; `step` completes the stop and\n   `stopped?` reports it.  A session without a node, or one already\n   stopping, is answered unchanged.  The board serves a read-only ring\n   that stop does not end, so a reader has nothing to be told but the\n   reattachable close its connection observes.\n\n   This composition is the one resource owner: a host asks once, here,\n   and never closes a board, a dial or the store itself\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  [session]\n  (let [node (:node session)]\n    (if (or (nil? node) (::stopping? node))\n      session\n      (do (doseq [[_ {:keys [dial]}] (get-in node [::follow :links])]\n            (when dial (head.board/close! dial)))\n          (assoc session :node\n                 (cond-> (assoc node ::stopping? true)\n                   (get-in node [::publisher :server])\n                   (update-in [::publisher :server] head.board/stop!)\n\n                   (::follow node)\n                   (assoc-in [::follow :links] {})))))))\n\n\n(defn stopped?\n  \"True when the head composition owes nothing at exit: no node, no\n   board server, or a board server that is stopped or refused.\"\n  [session]\n  (let [server (get-in session [:node ::publisher :server])]\n    (or (nil? server) (head.board/stopped? server))))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"The last resort after the exit drain's budget\n   (`yin.repl.main/stop-ticks`): whatever the board still owes is asked\n   for once more and not awaited.  The ordinary exit is `stop!`, then\n   `step` until `stopped?`.  A session never stopped is stopped first, so\n   a direct caller (a test, an embedder without a drain) still closes the\n   dials; the board's stopping tick runs at the node's last tick reading\n   only when the board is not already `stopped?`.\n\n   The store's own resources are the durable handle's `:close-fn`, which\n   the composition's single resource owner releases after this\n   (`yin.shell.main/close-composition!`), so nothing here is closed\n   twice.\"\n  [session]\n  (let [session (stop! session)\n        node (:node session)\n        server (get-in node [::publisher :server])]\n    (when (and server (not (head.board/stopped? server)))\n      (head.board/serve-step server (or (::now node) 0)))\n    nil))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n(ns dao.host.hash\n  \"The jolt override of src/cljc/dao/host/hash.cljc (the :jolt alias puts\n   src/jolt first, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.2, §6.2,\n   §6.3): the same public entries, arities, docstrings and refusal data\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A).\n\n   P entries (§2.4): `blake3-bytes` and `sha256-bytes`. They take host\n   bytes (jolt's byte array) and return fresh host bytes representing the\n   32-byte digest (256 bits). They leave their arguments unmodified.\n\n   Both are `:blocking` calls into native/jolt-crypto, which `bb\n   build:jolt-native` builds: BLAKE3 is the vendored upstream C reference,\n   SHA-256 the declared system libcrypto's EVP API. The input is copied into\n   caller-owned native memory (never a C string, so embedded NUL is data),\n   the digest is read back into a fresh jolt byte array, and the memory is\n   freed on every path: each native acquisition owns its own release,\n   established as soon as it is acquired (`with-native`), so a later\n   allocation or copy that fails still frees every earlier buffer, and each\n   free runs whether or not another failed.\n\n   Loading this namespace is the provenance gate (§6.3): it refuses, by\n   throwing, unless the wrapper writes this namespace's layout and reports\n   that every EVP entry resolved to exactly the library jolt-toolchain.edn\n   qualified for this platform (:native :libcrypto :qualified): the same\n   canonical real path (which the declared :path must also resolve to), the\n   same OpenSSL_version_num and the same file SHA-256, at no lower than\n   :min-version. An upgrade, a repointed link or a replaced file therefore\n   fails until requalified (the procedure is in jolt-toolchain.edn). No\n   digest is computed before that check passes; a missing library fails the\n   load.\n\n   String digesting is a table B portable composition over `dao.host.text`\n   and these byte primitives (`blake3`, `sha256`, `digest-string`,\n   `digest-bytes`), hosted in `dao.jing`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The native library and its provenance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private platform\n  ;; as yang.antlr.cst decides it: jolt's os.name/os.arch shim can answer\n  ;; nil, which reads as Linux and x86_64\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (or (System/getProperty \"os.name\") \"\"))\n        arch (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n    (str (if (str/includes? os \"mac\") \"darwin\" \"linux\") \"-\"\n         (if (#{\"aarch64\" \"arm64\"} arch) \"arm64\" \"x86_64\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private library\n  ;; the wrapper `bb build:jolt-native` builds, under the working directory\n  (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\") \"/build/native/\" platform\n       \"/jolt-crypto/lib/libjolt_crypto\"\n       (if (str/starts-with? platform \"darwin\") \".dylib\" \".so\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private libcrypto-declaration\n  (get-in (edn/read-string (slurp (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\")\n                                       \"/jolt-toolchain.edn\")))\n          [:native :libcrypto]))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library library)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-layout-version \"jolt_crypto_layout_version\" [] :int)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-provenance \"jolt_crypto_provenance\" [:pointer :size_t] :int)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-blake3 \"jolt_crypto_blake3\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-sha256 \"jolt_crypto_sha256\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n;; 3 (J2): the random entry joined the exported set (jolt_crypto_random for\n;; yin.vm.linker.sign/generate's :jolt arm); a J1b-built wrapper answers 2 and\n;; is refused here rather than at a missing-symbol error in the linker.\n;; 4 (J6c): jolt_crypto_sha1 joined it (dao.stream.ws.crypto) and EVP_sha1\n;; the provenance audit; a J2-built wrapper answers 3 and is refused here.\n(def ^:private layout 4)\n\n\n(defn- refuse-load\n  [message data]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt-crypto refused: \" message)\n                  (assoc data :library library))))\n\n\n(when-not (= layout (c-layout-version))\n  (refuse-load \"the library writes another layout\"\n               {:expected layout, :actual (c-layout-version)}))\n\n\n(defn- with-native\n  \"(f p) over caller-owned native memory `p` of `n` bytes (one for an empty\n   input), freed however `f` exits. The release is established before\n   anything else can fail, so nesting one call per acquisition frees each\n   buffer independently of the others.\"\n  [n f]\n  (let [p (ffi/alloc (max 1 n))]\n    (try\n      (when (ffi/null? p)\n        (throw (ex-info \"jolt-crypto native allocation failed\" {:bytes n})))\n      (f p)\n      (finally (ffi/free p)))))\n\n\n(defn- version-number\n  \"OpenSSL_version_num of a \\\"major.minor.patch\\\" text (OpenSSL 3's\n   0xMNN00PP0 form).\"\n  [text]\n  (let [[major minor patch] (map #(Long/parseLong %) (str/split text #\"\\.\"))]\n    (+ (bit-shift-left major 28) (bit-shift-left minor 20) (bit-shift-left patch 4))))\n\n\n(def ^:private provenance\n  (with-native 4096\n    (fn [buf]\n      (let [n (c-provenance buf 4096)]\n        (when (neg? n)\n          (refuse-load \"libcrypto provenance unavailable\" {:status n}))\n        (let [[num text path digest] (str/split (ffi/read-bytes buf n) #\"\\t\")]\n          {:version-num (Long/parseLong num), :version text, :path path,\n           :sha256 digest})))))\n\n\n(defn- canonical\n  [path]\n  (.getCanonicalPath (java.io.File. ^String path)))\n\n\n(let [declared (get-in libcrypto-declaration [:path (keyword platform)])\n      qualified (get-in libcrypto-declaration [:qualified (keyword platform)])\n      minimum (:min-version libcrypto-declaration)\n      refuse (fn [message]\n               (refuse-load message {:declared declared, :qualified qualified,\n                                     :provenance provenance}))]\n  (when-not (and declared qualified minimum)\n    (refuse \"jolt-toolchain.edn qualifies no libcrypto for this platform\"))\n  ;; canonical paths: dyld answers the real path behind Homebrew's opt/\n  ;; link, and a Linux loader may name the file through /lib\n  (when-not (= (canonical (:path provenance)) (:canonical-path qualified))\n    (refuse \"EVP resolved to an undeclared libcrypto (canonical path differs from the qualified one)\"))\n  (when-not (= (canonical declared) (:canonical-path qualified))\n    (refuse \"the declared libcrypto path resolves to another file than the qualified one (repointed)\"))\n  (when-not (= (:version-num provenance) (:version-num qualified))\n    (refuse \"libcrypto version differs from the qualified one (upgrade or downgrade)\"))\n  (when-not (= (:sha256 provenance) (:sha256 qualified))\n    (refuse \"libcrypto file digest differs from the qualified one (replaced)\"))\n  (when (< (:version-num provenance) (version-number minimum))\n    (refuse \"libcrypto is older than the declared minimum\")))\n\n\n(defn- digest\n  \"The 32-byte result of wrapper entry `c-fn` over `bs`, copied into a fresh\n   jolt byte array.\"\n  [entry c-fn bs]\n  (let [n (alength bs)]\n    (with-native n\n      (fn [in]\n        (when (pos? n) (ffi/write-array in bs))\n        (with-native 32\n          (fn [out]\n            (let [status (c-fn in n out)]\n              (when-not (zero? status)\n                (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt-crypto \" entry \" failed\")\n                                {:entry entry, :status status})))\n              (ffi/read-array out 32))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The profile surface\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- check-bytes!\n  [entry bs]\n  (when-not (bytes/bytes? bs)\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" unsupported-value (expected host bytes)\")\n                    {:dao.host/refusal :unsupported-value\n                     :dao.host/entry entry}))))\n\n\n(defn blake3-bytes\n  \"P. 32-byte BLAKE3 digest of host bytes `bs`, returning fresh host bytes.\"\n  [bs]\n  (check-bytes! 'blake3-bytes bs)\n  (digest 'blake3-bytes c-blake3 bs))\n\n\n(defn sha256-bytes\n  \"P. 32-byte SHA-256 digest of host bytes `bs`, returning fresh host bytes.\"\n  [bs]\n  (check-bytes! 'sha256-bytes bs)\n  (digest 'sha256-bytes c-sha256 bs))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
