{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git diff --name-only origin/master..HEAD; sed -n '315,350p' collab/jolt/1794773141000-architect-j7-design.findings.md; sed -n '1,35p' test/resources/yin/repl/jolt-applicability.edn; sed -n '1,85p' src/jolt/dao/posix/random.jolt; date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC'\"","aggregated_output":"collab/jolt/1794773141000-architect-j7-design.findings.md\ncollab/jolt/1794775739000-engineer-j7-impl.findings.md\ncollab/jolt/j7-review-prompt.md\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/udp/common.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc\nsrc/jolt/dao/posix/random.jolt\nsrc/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt\nsrc/jolt/yin/vm/linker/random.jolt\nreported as partial, but §10.1's J7 gate remains open.\n\n## 6. J0b regressions retained\n\n`bb probe:jolt-udp` already exists (`bb.edn:70`), driving tracked\n`src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.{clj,sh}`. Preserve its assertions and diagnostic\nrecords. The old shell wrapper can fall back to an ignored spike checkout;\nJ7 qualification must explicitly use the bootstrapped tracked toolchain and\nrecord its SHA/clean state rather than relying on that fallback.\n\n| §8.3 leg | Retained proof / evidence required for J7 |\n|---|---|\n| 1 — boundaries | Nonblocking loopback bind and ephemeral-port readback; exact payload AND source for empty, embedded-NUL, consecutive distinct, and N-sized packets; one receive consumes at most one packet. Inject short send: error, no suffix send and no accepted packet. Repeat through production helpers and the public writer. |\n| 2 — bounds | N=1200 and configured N=8192, asserting the latter is below the measured send maximum; N, N+1 and packets larger than the receive buffer. No accepted prefix, consumed oversize packet leaves no remainder. Separately induce above-platform-limit EMSGSIZE and observe no delivery. Preserve platform header/sysctl/MTU and socket-buffer readback evidence. Add IPv6 coverage in J7 without pretending it existed in J0b. |\n| 3 — pressure | Raw would-block classification retains errno. Inject target EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK and ENOBUFS with zero accepted packets; also exercise actual successful syscalls before/after. Natural pressure trials remain RECORD observations, including packet loss; no requirement to manufacture natural loopback EAGAIN. At the public writer assert transport-error plus send-failed, no `full`, no wait and no replay on later turns. |\n| 4 — readiness / cleanup | Keep the distinct raw probe's read waiter: it parks through the poller, another fiber progresses, a packet wakes it, cancel releases it, close/forget removes descriptor state, post-close receive reports EBADF. The harness may wait/retry to make observations; those loops must not enter production `append!` or receive turns. Test production failed-open cleanup, repeated close, no retained fd/native buffers and descriptor reuse separately. |\n| 5 — reproducibility | Separate macOS arm64/Linux x86_64 records: repository and runtime SHA, Chez/compiler/native provenance, platform and header constants, exact command/exit, packet sizes/counts, raw error traces, injected vs natural labels, poller traces and final empty ownership state. Missing machine/output is incomplete, not passed. |\n\nHistorical evidence exists, not a fresh acceptance result:\n\n- [macOS round 2](1792429967000-engineer-jolt-j0b-udp-probe-r2.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md)\n  records 36 passing assertions and three observations on jolt `96d7b866`;\n  IPv4 maximum observed there was 9216 bytes.\n- [Linux review/sign-off](1792487422000-reviewer-jolt-j0b-linux.qwen3.8-max.findings.md)\n  records shiva runs with 37 passing assertions and three observations,\n  maximum 65507 and EMSGSIZE 90. The extra assertion is Linux SO_SNDBUF\n  readback. Both platforms used injection for send pressure/short-send paths.\n- [tracked probe transfer](1792489765000-engineer-jolt-j0b-commit-prep.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md)\n  records the move into `src/dev`. The governing table's old J0b\n  “probe-only; not merged” label is not evidence the tracked files are absent,\n  and the old runs are not datagram/DHT conformance.\n\nCurrent `jolt-toolchain.edn` pins `b389f1a7fb553f63a3494d71f8fe3251790bf4d3`,\nnot the probe's historical SHA (nor the older SHA in `src/jolt/README.md`).\nRerun the retained legs at the actual qualified pin on both platforms.\nThe J6 macOS Autobahn waiver does not waive J7 UDP or signed-head evidence.\n;; Per-deftest exclusions on jolt (J3, amended by J4d: no J4-owned entry\n;; remains; each J7 entry composes a dht: store; amended by J5: no J5-owned\n;; entry remains, Python runs over the native C++ parser). The JVM runs each\n;; original body unchanged.\n;; Namespace exclusions live in src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj.\n{:test-exclusions [{:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"a-key-file-loads-the-stable-key-or-refuses-startup-with-its-reason\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"declared-principals-are-strict-hex-and-reach-the-composition\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"trusted-principals-are-strict-and-apart-from-declared-ones\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"dht-join-expands-a-token-to-peer-principal-and-follow\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"a-printed-join-token-is-what-join-parses\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"dht-follow-of-an-undeclared-principal-refuses-startup\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"dht-manifest-suspends-following-for-the-run\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"dht-init-publishes-with-a-key-and-localhost-peer\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"dht-serve-fetches-only\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"codec-flag-selects-the-served-wire-profile\"\n                    :reason \"J6 Transit capability unavailable in J3\" :capability \"J6 Transit\" :owner \"J6\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"with-the-dht-store-still-hydrating-a-renewal-and-a-pending-release-are-still-sent-test\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.state-test\" :test \"dht-join-saves-its-follow-and-a-bare-start-resumes-it\"\n                    :reason \"composes a dht: index store, which needs the UDP transport (J4d run: fails only at that refusal)\" :capability \"J7 DHT transport\" :owner \"J7\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"a-dart-client-attaches-to-this-jvm-server\"\n                    :reason \"JVM socket fixture; portable injected endpoints remain active\" :capability \"JVM WebSocket peers\" :owner \"J6\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"killing-the-connection-is-observable-and-requests-are-lost\"\n                    :reason \"JVM socket fixture; portable injected endpoints remain active\" :capability \"JVM WebSocket peers\" :owner \"J6\"}\n                   {:ns \"yin.repl.main-test\" :test \"stopping-the-endpoint-ends-the-served-stream-not-closes-it\"\n                    :reason \"JVM socket fixture; portable injected endpoints remain active\" :capability \"JVM WebSocket peers\" :owner \"J6\"}\n(ns dao.posix.random\n  \"Fresh-entropy adapter for jolt drawing random bytes from the qualified\n   libcrypto CSPRNG wrapper (jolt_crypto_random).\n   dao.space and yin.vm both use this seam.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    [dao.host.hash]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n(def ^:private library\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (or (System/getProperty \"os.name\") \"\"))\n        arch (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")\n        darwin? (str/includes? os \"mac\")]\n    (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\") \"/build/native/\"\n         (if darwin? \"darwin\" \"linux\") \"-\"\n         (if (#{\"aarch64\" \"arm64\"} arch) \"arm64\" \"x86_64\")\n         \"/jolt-crypto/lib/libjolt_crypto\" (if darwin? \".dylib\" \".so\"))))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library library)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-random \"jolt_crypto_random\"\n            [:pointer :size_t] :int :blocking)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-cleanse \"jolt_crypto_cleanse\" [:pointer :size_t] :void)\n\n\n(defn rand-bytes\n  \"A fresh jolt byte array of `n` random bytes (n >= 0) from the qualified\n   libcrypto's CSPRNG. Randomness failure is an error: a nonzero wrapper\n   status throws.\"\n  [n]\n  (when (neg? n)\n    (throw (ex-info \"dao.posix.random/rand-bytes negative count\" {:n n})))\n  (let [size (max 1 n)\n        p (ffi/alloc size)]\n    (try\n      (when (ffi/null? p)\n        (throw (ex-info \"jolt-crypto native allocation failed\" {:bytes n})))\n      (let [status (c-random p n)]\n        (when-not (zero? status)\n          (throw (ex-info \"jolt-crypto random failed\" {:entry 'rand-bytes\n                                                       :status status})))\n        (if (pos? n) (ffi/read-array p n) (bytes/alloc 0)))\n      (finally\n        (try (c-cleanse p size)\n             (finally (ffi/free p)))))))\n2026-11-15 20:55:38 UTC\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"Fault injection confirmed three defects: failed close-on-exec or IPv6-only setup still reports `bound`; a setup exception leaves the acquired descriptor unclosed; and a persistent receive `ENOTSOCK` error is silently retried on later turns. Send-pressure and short-send checks passed, as did 920 signed-head and follower assertions over the shared test mesh. I’m writing the findings now.\n"}}
